<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">keyring</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">keyring</ansi> command tracks your current keys and picked locks. 

Whenever you use a key, it is taken from your items and added to your keyring 
forever. You cannot lose a key once this happens.

If you pick a lock, you remember its sequence until the server restarts. Until
then the lock opens at once when you go through that exit or open that
container. A restart changes every lock, so you must pick it again.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

::rows
  <ansi fg="command">keyring</ansi>  This will list all keys and lockpick sequences you have.
           It will tell you the Type, Location, exit or container name, and 
           as the lockpick sequence if applicable.
::

<ansi fg="yellow">Example: </ansi>

    <ansi fg="black-bold">[HP:66/66 MP:35/35]:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">keyring</ansi>
::keep
    <ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="table-title">Your Keyring:</ansi>
::
::rows
    <ansi fg="white-bold">Type</ansi>      <ansi fg="white-bold">Location</ansi>, <ansi fg="white-bold">Where</ansi>, <ansi fg="white-bold">Sequence</ansi>
    <ansi fg="white-bold">Key</ansi>       <ansi fg="magenta">#110 Inside of the Catacombs</ansi>, <ansi fg="exit">west</ansi>, <ansi fg="black-bold">-</ansi>
    <ansi fg="white-bold">Lockpick</ansi>  <ansi fg="magenta">#784 Inside a Residence</ansi>, <ansi fg="container">chest</ansi>, <ansi fg="green-bold">D U U</ansi>
::

::rows
<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi>  <ansi fg="command">help picklock</ansi>
::
